# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF (two coupling subspaces), FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE,
# now including C4_SPINOR (4-component DHF) alongside NON_REL and X2C in one run.
#
# For C4_DHF, orbital rotations are restricted to the positive-energy spinors only: rotating an
# occupied positive-energy orbital into the negative-energy (Dirac sea) branch is exactly the
# min-max saddle-point direction relativistic SCF is characterized by (Talman, Phys. Rev. Lett.
# 57, 1091 (1986); Saue, ChemPhysChem 12, 3077 (2011)) -- allowing it would let the energy
# decrease without bound (variational collapse). Excluding those pairs from the parameter space
# entirely (not merely leaving them at zero gradient) keeps the no-pair approximation exact and
# turns C4_DHF's own orbital optimization into an ordinary MINIMIZATION, same as NON_REL/X2C
# (watch for "rotations excluded from the N negative-energy (Dirac sea) spinors" in the log, and
# the final "[PASS] the point is a genuine minimum" from NEO's own post-loop Hessian check on
# lih_gnof_c4_neo_full_optimization.inp). C4_DHF's positive-energy branch is itself Kramers-paired
# the same way X2C's spinors are, so it is Kramers-restricted here too.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
